Although this is not yet implemented anywhere but autocorrecting parsers
will autoinsert {cu} after cmevla in clauses (bridi) where the main selbri
is absent.
e.g. {la lojban. mo} is {la .lojban. cu mo} since no other selbri is
present. However,
{la moxamed morsi cu mo} will treat the name as consisting of two words
since the selbri is already present.

This will allow to correctly parse most sentences of do-not-merge and
do-merge communities.

Actually this is not the largest problem in the live corpus. The largest
problem is plain wrong Lojban of newcomers.

